.TH tkufiletree n 0.1 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkufiletree
.PP
A lazy file\-system tree built on \fBtkutils::tkutree\fR. Shows a directory hierarchy under a root; subdirectories are read from disk only when expanded (no full walk). Files can be filtered by glob patterns, and activating a file fires a callback with its full path. Tk 8.6+ and 9.x.
.SS API
.CS
::tkutils::tkufiletree::widget       path ?options?
::tkutils::tkufiletree::setRoot      path dir
::tkutils::tkufiletree::refresh      path
::tkutils::tkufiletree::up           path        ;# re-root to parent dir
::tkutils::tkufiletree::selectedPath path        ;# full path or ""
::tkutils::tkufiletree::root         path        ;# current root dir or ""
::tkutils::tkufiletree::reveal       path target  ;# expand+select a path
::tkutils::tkufiletree::treeview     path        ;# raw ttk::treeview
.CE
.PP
\fBreveal\fR expands the directory chain down to \fBtarget\fR (a path under the root), selects it and scrolls it into view, populating ancestors as needed. If the exact target is not a node (e.g. excluded by the filter), the deepest existing ancestor — its folder — is selected instead. It returns 1 when the exact target was selected, else 0, and never raises. Together with \fBroot\fR and \fBsetRoot\fR this lets a host application keep the tree pointing at — and highlighting — whatever it just opened elsewhere. \fBup\fR re\-roots to the parent directory (also bound to \fBBackSpace\fR) and reveals the previous root.
.SS "Options (widget)"
.IP \(bu
\fB\-root dir\fR — starting directory (default: current directory).
.IP \(bu
\fB\-filter {pat ...}\fR — glob patterns; only matching files are shown (directories are always shown). Empty = all files. Case\-insensitive.
.IP \(bu
\fB\-files 0|1\fR — show files at all (default 1; 0 = directories only).
.IP \(bu
\fB\-showhidden 0|1\fR — include dot\-entries (default 0).
.IP \(bu
\fB\-onactivate cmd\fR — called with the full path when a file is activated (double\-click or Return).
.IP \(bu
\fB\-onselect cmd\fR — called with the full path on selection change.
.IP \(bu
\fB\-height n\fR — visible rows (default 16).
.IP \(bu
\fB\-isolatekeys 0|1\fR — when 1, drop the toplevel from the tree's bindtags so a host application's global key bindings do not also fire while the tree has focus (default 0). Keyboard navigation, expand/collapse and \fBBackSpace\fR (go up) stay local to the tree.
.PP
Item ids are the normalized full paths, so \fBselectedPath\fR and the callbacks hand back ready\-to\-use paths.
.SS Example
.CS
package require tkutils::tkufiletree
set t [::tkutils::tkufiletree::widget .t \
          -root [pwd] -filter {*.png *.jpg *.gif *.bmp} \
          -onactivate {apply {p {puts "open: $p"}}}]
pack $t -fill both -expand 1
.CE
.SS Demo
.CS
tclsh examples/demo-tkufiletree.tcl ?startdir?
.CE
